OL,3,GNEWSANorfolk rig worker stuck in Gabon
OL,4,Aafter disaster
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe fiancee of an offshore worker who
OL,7,Fsurvived the sinking of a drilling rig
OL,8,Foff the west coast of Africa in which
OL,9,Ffour people died says she fears for his
OL,10,Fmental health as he cannot come home.
OL,12,FRig worker Will Bracken, 39, from Great
OL,13,FYarmouth, Norfolk, helped navigate a
OL,14,Flifeboat which he said carried 47 men
OL,15,Fto shore when the Prospector 5 sank off
OL,16,FMayumba, Gabon, on 24 October.
OL,18,FHis fiancee Danielle Bullent says he is
OL,19,Fone of several British workers at a
OL,20,Fsecure hotel complex in Port-Gentil who
OL,21,Fare not permitted to leave while an
OL,22,Finvestigation gets under way.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,377,370,200,160,0,100
